{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-spaces-from-equivalence-relations}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c23f910105858bf397f5af66115ae9a6d35fa75083ee58e2bd557adf2dbe993f", "source_text": "Algebraic spaces and equivalence relations", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aaad198bd8838d0a8912acce304a6f7f6702c293b0b0c2371334205f330a7a9c", "unit_id": "tag:0264:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$U/R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{groupoids-definition-quotient-sheaf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-algebraic-space}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e7594652d788330d98c1407aa1ec889c7dded103e9a77112e928260787e6438d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:90dd6a10e7c28d437e1610fa878bd4799a8aacc7ffb63f899205e47d202c4ad3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSuppose given a scheme <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002>\nand an <ACCENT_0001>tale equivalence relation <MATH_0003> on <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005>.\nWe would like to show this defines an algebraic space.\nWe will produce a series of lemmas that prove the quotient sheaf <MATH_0006>\n(see Groupoids, Definition <REF_0001>)\nhas all the properties required\nof it in Definition <REF_0002>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bed8488eb6e6d01792697ea5caf491acd2061d45be49dd38ced61e53b6eb4f41", "unit_id": "tag:0264:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j = (s, t) : R \\to U \\times_S U$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0008": "$R'$", "MATH_0009": "$R$", "MATH_0010": "$U'$", "MATH_0011": "$j' : R' \\to U' \\times_S U'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{groupoids-definition-restrict-relation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pullback-etale-equivalence-relation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2910e4a83dca3587bd7cd6a9a6b2c7f3ba5de74a4e7e71e630699ade354e46f1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9ab6e204bd2e2a56d0e11a8067135ae5a2eaaf4adf7e809c7ce2dd164d930909", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a scheme over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004>\nbe an <ACCENT_0001>tale equivalence relation on <MATH_0005> over <MATH_0006>.\nLet <MATH_0007> be an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism.\nLet <MATH_0008> be the restriction of <MATH_0009> to <MATH_0010>, see\nGroupoids, Definition <REF_0001>.\nThen <MATH_0011> is an <ACCENT_0003>tale equivalence\nrelation also.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3b681e2e210525af31a3f7a26ea36ea6cbc71c4749c9b71088f4741bd12f189", "unit_id": "tag:02WT:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$s', t'$", "MATH_0002": "$s' , t' : R' \\to U'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{groupoids-lemma-restrict-groupoid}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-etale}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-composition-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8a48d69640c5d10cf8a68f01d57782b441ee51427c8c80b945812dabf50b56e7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44ec9ed92f092c5d8efb676c7b2f9f69d311f061d037db6df72184362de2d6fd", "source_text": "It is clear from the description of <MATH_0001> in\nGroupoids, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthat <MATH_0002> are <ACCENT_0001>tale\nas compositions of base changes of <ACCENT_0002>tale morphisms\n(see Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0002>\nand <REF_0003>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bfcc4349ebe8bdbf5ca7b3f8d0586a22239fff9eb7c78d7ecf89c0fc7573d8d8", "unit_id": "tag:02WT:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{bootstrap-lemma-better-finding-opens}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:20478da8397bc6a3dc35640c41f4c172667ba01dae282bd8a65972b4aa2d9f3c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe will often use the following lemma to find open subspaces of algebraic\nspaces. A slight improvement (with more general hypotheses) of this lemma is\nBootstrap, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:694eb193602e4637240ef66aceca156a5254b676431170bf733b088aa1571b55", "unit_id": "tag:0264:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0264", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$U$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j = (s, t) : R \\to U \\times_S U$", "MATH_0005": "$g : U' \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$j$", "MATH_0007": "$s, t : R \\to U$", "MATH_0008": "$g$", "MATH_0009": "$R' = R|_{U'}$", "MATH_0010": "$R$", "MATH_0011": "$U'$", "MATH_0012": "$U'/R' \\to U/R$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finding-opens}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c05801501614e82e23850d1cc3488afb780d5fec3c385f16928d1bd5bfb3c384", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e492f6bbf4342142e1542c898c72d9cc2f69533154bfda2b8439b14aea71b3a0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a morphism.\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0006> is an equivalence relation,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0007> are surjective, flat and\nlocally of finite presentation,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0008> is flat and locally of finite presentation.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nLet <MATH_0009> be the restriction of <MATH_0010> to <MATH_0011>. Then\n<MATH_0012> is representable, and is an open immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:464517611d9f948983b34730145e46a6e528597a3f7e0dbb56faf3ab06e5693f", "unit_id": "tag:02WU:statement"}
